   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the state of New York bond bank agency to provide municipal\nrelief to the city of Albany",
    "basePrintNo": "S6922",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6922-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Albany, City of",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6922\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the state of New York bond bank agency to provide\nmunicipal relief to the city of Albany\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends the Laws of New York 2020, Chapter 56, Part H, Section 5, Page\n38, Line 16 to change the date of such transfer to be made as soon as\npracticable from March 31, 2021, to no later than December 31, 2021.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAs of now, the City of Albany has not been made whole on the $12m in\nCapital City Funding owed to the City in 2020, because the legislative\nauthorization for it expired in 2020. The State Department of Budget\nwithheldor $1.2 million, last year for fears of the fallout of the\npandemic. This bill aims to correct this problem with a legislative fix.\nSimply changing the date to December 31, 2021 allows the city to be made\nwhole. The legislation also allows the New York State Director of the\nBudget to request additional information from the city of Albany regard-\ning the utilization of these funds and the finances and operations of\nthe city, as appropriate.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
